---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { APP_CONFIG } from '../data/appData';
---

<Layout
  title={`Terms of Service — ${APP_CONFIG.name}`}
  description={`Terms of service for Syntac Android coding agent. Information regarding local execution, AI provider keys, licenses, and software usage.`}
>
  <div class="py-16 sm:py-24 relative z-10">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <div class="space-y-4 border-b border-[#8296DC]/12 pb-8">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-[#6684FF]/10 text-[#91A7FF] border border-[#6684FF]/25">
          <span>Legal & Disclaimers</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-[#F8FAFF]">
          Terms of Service
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#667085] font-mono">
          Last updated: February 28, 2025 • Version {APP_CONFIG.currentVersion}
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Main Terms Content -->
      <div class="glass-surface-card rounded-3xl p-8 sm:p-10 border border-[#8296DC]/15 space-y-8 text-sm text-[#9EA8B8] leading-relaxed">
        
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F8FAFF]">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
          <p>
            By downloading, installing, compiling, or using <strong>Syntac</strong> (the "Application"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, do not install or use the Application.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F8FAFF]">2. Local Execution and Device Responsibility</h2>
          <p>
            Syntac executes commands, edits files, and manages containers directly on your physical Android device. You acknowledge and accept that:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[#F8FAFF]/90">
            <li>Syntac runs file modification tools (e.g., <code>edit</code>, <code>write</code>, <code>delete</code>) on your local filesystem based on AI prompts and autonomous loops.</li>
            <li>Shell commands executed via the Arch Linux PRoot runtime or Termux bridge run with the permissions of your Android user space.</li>
            <li>You are solely responsible for maintaining backups of your source code and device data before executing automated coding tasks.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F8FAFF]">3. Third-Party AI Providers & API Usage</h2>
          <p>
            Syntac connects to third-party AI providers (such as Google Cloud Code Assist, DeepSeek, OpenRouter, and custom endpoints) using credentials you supply.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[#F8FAFF]/90">
            <li>Your interactions with third-party providers are governed by their respective terms of service and privacy policies.</li>
            <li>You are responsible for all API usage fees, token consumption costs, and quota limits associated with your personal API accounts.</li>
            <li>Syntac does not guarantee the availability, uptime, or output accuracy of any third-party AI provider.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F8FAFF]">4. Early Access Beta & Disclaimer of Warranty</h2>
          <p>
            The Application is provided on an <strong>"AS IS"</strong> and <strong>"AS AVAILABLE"</strong> basis during its beta development cycle. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the developer (<strong>DraxonV1</strong>) disclaims all warranties, express or implied, including but not limited to fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, or freedom from software bugs.
          </p>
          <p>
            Under no circumstances shall the developer or contributors be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages resulting from the use or inability to use the Application, including lost code, data corruption, or hardware malfunction.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F8FAFF]">5. Open-Source Source Code & Intellectual Property</h2>
          <p>
            The Syntac source code is publicly accessible on GitHub at <a href={APP_CONFIG.repoUrl} class="text-[#91A7FF] underline">{APP_CONFIG.repoUrl}</a>. All code generated by the AI agent on your device belongs entirely to you. Syntac claims no ownership or license over your projects or outputs.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F8FAFF]">6. Modifications to Terms</h2>
          <p>
            These terms may be updated alongside new releases of Syntac. Continued use of the Application following any updates constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <div class="pt-6 border-t border-[#8296DC]/10 flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-[#667085]">
          <span>Syntac Project</span>
          <a href={APP_CONFIG.repoUrl} class="text-[#91A7FF] hover:underline">GitHub Repository</a>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
